 <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 06:50:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 134/154] atrium(links): download an option-click when no peek
 controller exists
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
index 484a364276a53..00bee363c8f36 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
@@ -1546,9 +1546,17 @@ WebContents* Browser::OpenURLFromTab(
   // never, so shift+click fell through to a stock new window. The peek card
   // itself is C++ and survived, so the gate goes and the feature returns.
   if (params.disposition == WindowOpenDisposition::NEW_WINDOW &&
-      params.is_renderer_initiated && !params.started_from_context_menu &&
-      atrium::MaybeOpenPeek(this, source, params.url, params.referrer)) {
-    return source;  // No new WebContents/window created on this path.
+      params.is_renderer_initiated && !params.started_from_context_menu) {
+    if (atrium::MaybeOpenPeek(this, source, params.url, params.referrer)) {
+      return source;  // No new WebContents/window created on this path.
+    }
+    // No controller for this window (a popup, DevTools, or app window) -
+    // Option alone reaches here the same as Shift, and upstream's answer to
+    // an unpeekable Option-click is a download, not a new window.
+    if (atrium::OptionOnlyModifierHeld()) {
+      atrium::DownloadOptionClickedLink(source, params);
+      return source;  // No new WebContents/window created on this path.
+    }
   }
   // Auto-peek for a plain click lives in AtriumPeekNavigationThrottle, since
   // a plain click emits no OpenURL IPC. A window.open with noopener does,
